<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    Templated from VFEP's VFEP_WarcasketHelmet_Siegebreaker (VFEP v3.09,
    1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Misc/Apparel_Headgear.xml); fields not discussed here, uiIconScale and
    the psychic and toxic offsets included, are Siegebreaker's. Plating, tags and the
    market-value references follow the armor's header, as does the art note.

    Tuning: ComponentSpacer 4 / Plasteel 60 (Siegebreaker 2 / 50, Sarcophagus 2 / 60, Controller
    and Brute 4 / 60): the components are the tier's price for a helmet with a function of its
    own, the plasteel the utility sets'. 1340 silver at market value.

    The medic offsets, the diagnostic visor:
    - MedicalTendQuality +0.10, one Medicine level, a hospital bed's offset; reaches the
      mechanite dressing through vanilla's tend formula and a normal tend alike.
    - MedicalSurgerySuccessChance +0.05, the hospital hook: small because any spacer armor can
      take this helmet and vanilla's own precedent is the hospital bed's x1.1 factor.
    - Sight floor 0.7 through the ApparelExtension, the tier's floor for the region the visor
      covers (no VFEP armor floors Sight, so this one counts). A floor never lowers a capacity;
      it feeds both tend stats through their Sight factor and steadies an impaired pilot's aim.
      The 1.0 floor is Sarcophagus's identity, left to that set's helmet for a mix-and-match
      pilot who wants it.
    - The mechanite dressing (armor) treats diseases and infections, not just wounds, only
      while this helmet is worn by the pilot; the check is a def comparison in
      Ability_MechaniteDressing (the Controller helmet idiom). The description's first
      paragraph says so.

    ApparelExtension priority 1, for the reason in the armor def's header: the
    VFEP_WarcasketHelmetBase parent carries its own, and only the highest-priority copy keeps
    its fields whole (Merge still ORs the parent's isUnifiedApparel and hideHead in). Any new
    ApparelExtension field for this piece goes on this entry.

    Compat: SOS2Patch.xml gives it the EVA tag and Insulation_Cold 100 alongside the armor;
    the VGE vacuum patch lowers its VacuumResistance to VGE1's warcasket-helmet value.
  -->
  <VFEPirates.WarcasketDef ParentName="VFEP_WarcasketHelmetBase">
    <defName>MDWC_WarcasketHelmet_Medic</defName>
    <label>medic warcasket helmet</label>
    <shortDescription>Specialized spacer-tech warcasket helmet with standard protection, fitted with a diagnostic visor that lets the mechanite dressing treat disease and infection as well as wounds.</shortDescription>
    <description>Specialized spacer-tech warcasket helmet with standard protection, fitted with a diagnostic visor that lets the mechanite dressing treat disease and infection as well as wounds.\n\nA 10th-generation spacer chassis refitted for the medic's role: the pilot is welded in for good, like any warcasket wearer, but this one is built to keep the rest of the squad alive rather than to break the line.\n\nThe medic series trades firepower for the tools to treat wounds under fire, so a squad that fields one can stay in the fight long after its stims and bandages have run out.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketMedic/WarcasketMedicHelmet</texPath>
      <shaderType>CutoutComplex</shaderType>
    </graphicData>
    <uiIconScale>1.25</uiIconScale>
    <statBases>
      <Mass>8</Mass>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>2</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>1</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>1</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <Insulation_Cold>5</Insulation_Cold>
      <Insulation_Heat>2</Insulation_Heat>
      <EquipDelay>1</EquipDelay>
    </statBases>
    <equippedStatOffsets>
      <PsychicSensitivity>-0.5</PsychicSensitivity>
      <ToxicResistance>0.5</ToxicResistance>
      <MedicalTendQuality>0.10</MedicalTendQuality>
      <MedicalSurgerySuccessChance>0.05</MedicalSurgerySuccessChance>
      <SlaveSuppressionOffset MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">0.1</SlaveSuppressionOffset>
      <VacuumResistance MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">0.7</VacuumResistance>
    </equippedStatOffsets>
    <costList>
      <ComponentSpacer>4</ComponentSpacer>
      <Plasteel>60</Plasteel>
    </costList>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>VFEP_SpacerWarcaskets</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <apparel>
      <bodyPartGroups>
        <li>FullHead</li>
      </bodyPartGroups>
      <wornGraphicPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketMedic/WarcasketMedicHelmet</wornGraphicPath>
      <useWornGraphicMask>true</useWornGraphicMask>
      <layers>
        <li>Overhead</li>
      </layers>
      <tags>
        <li>WarcasketVeteran</li>
        <li>WarcasketAll</li>
      </tags>
    </apparel>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VEF.Apparels.ApparelExtension">
        <priority>1</priority>
        <pawnCapacityMinLevels>
          <li>
            <capacity>Sight</capacity>
            <minLevel>0.7</minLevel>
          </li>
        </pawnCapacityMinLevels>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VFEPirates.WarcasketDef>
</Defs>
